{
  "A": "Research a low-overhead, order-preserving streaming implementation. Retain the original Heap permutation sequence. Check vertex counts and identity before expensive preprocessing; add necessary rejection using sorted vertex signatures comprising loop status and adjacency-row population count. Derive these from the constructed graph, not raw edge counts, because duplicate edges collapse. Compare flat byte adjacency against packed storage. Maintain the number of loop/degree-incompatible assignments in O(1) per swap, invoking exact adjacency verification only when that count is zero. Preserve early-exit verification rather than assuming full mismatch maintenance is faster. Disable unnecessary iostream synchronization and replace per-line flushing with bounded buffering, preserving exact output bytes. Deliver the best independently correct measured variant; this tree supplies a simple streaming fallback and reusable low-overhead infrastructure.",
  "B": "Research factorial pruning that preserves Heap output order directly. Express the given iterative generator as equivalent recursive blocks: a size-k block permutes the first k positions while its suffix remains fixed. Reject blocks when fixed assignments violate loops, vertex invariants, edges or nonedges, or when a remaining vertex has no compatible unused target. Evaluate collision-safe joint color refinement across both graphs, with shared color identifiers and color-class histogram rejection; colors are necessary constraints, never proof of isomorphism. Critical requirement: skipping a block must still apply its exact terminal permutation before traversal continues. Derive and precompute these transformations by composition without enumerating k! leaves or storing factorial-sized integers. Preserve traversal order, enumerate every surviving mapping, and verify exact adjacency at completion. Measure lightweight pruning against stronger refinement/domain checks rather than assuming additional pruning pays for its overhead.",
  "C": "Research constraint-driven enumeration with exact output-order restoration. After the identity fast path, enumerate bijections using most-constrained-vertex selection, loop/color compatibility, and forward checking of both adjacency and nonadjacency. Do not stop at the first solution or discard automorphically equivalent mappings: the reference requires them all. For each complete mapping, derive its exact position in the reference Heap traversal using recursive block-entry states and mixed-radix branch-index keys. Prove equivalence to the supplied iterative generator; ordinary lexicographic mapping order is wrong, and fixed-width factorial ranks overflow for valid sizes. Sort completed mappings by these keys before emitting. Bound collection memory; if the bound is exceeded, discard the unprinted collection and restart through a correct streaming Heap implementation. Compare stronger variable-ordering benefits against ranking, sorting, preprocessing and fallback overhead.",
  "G": "Integrate only programs and components produced by A/B/C. Preserve each best standalone candidate and compare it with every proposed integration under the unchanged correctness and timing harness. Start with A's fast paths, representation and buffering combined separately with B's ordered pruning or C's enumeration/restoration; do not assume their gains add or blindly combine both search engines. Audit identity-only output, complete nonidentity mapping enumeration, exact Heap ordering, loops, duplicate edges, unequal sizes, failure text, and storage beyond 64 vertices. Keep bounded-memory fallbacks and avoid factorial overflow. Require correctness before considering timing, and interpret small differences against the observed timing spread using repetitions already permitted by the experiment. Select the best measured valid program, even if it is an unmerged tree candidate or the baseline. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target or permissions.",
  "analysis": "Only Problem A and src/brute_isomorphism.cpp are relevant. The sole measured baseline passed four cases and averaged 8.224 ms, with samples spanning 8.132–8.336 ms. There is no profile establishing search dominance, a particular graph family, or a benefit from parallelism. Prioritize portable, low-overhead CPU algorithms on the four-core ARM64 target; no GPU is available. The decisive semantic constraint is the source's unusual output: identity succeeds immediately and prints only identity; otherwise execution continues through Heap's entire permutation sequence and prints every isomorphism in that order. Returning one arbitrary mapping is therefore unsafe. Preserve trailing spaces, newlines and the exact failure message. Self-loops participate in verification, repeated edges collapse into Boolean adjacency, and valid graphs can exceed 64 vertices. The portfolio separates low-risk execution improvements, order-preserving search pruning, and stronger constraint search with explicit order restoration. All proposed gains remain hypotheses until measured."
}